# macforge secrets — 1Password reference file.
#
# This file is SAFE to commit: it holds only op:// references, never real values.
# 1Password resolves each reference at runtime; nothing secret is written to disk.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Copy to your machine-local path:  cp ~/.config/macforge/secrets.env.example ~/.config/macforge/secrets.env
#   2. Replace each op:// reference with the real vault/item/field from your 1Password.
#   3. Run any command that needs these secrets with the `oprun` helper (see shell/functions/secrets):
#          oprun mix phx.server
#          oprun -- ./some-script.sh
#      or directly:
#          op run --env-file="$HOME/.config/macforge/secrets.env" -- <command>
#
# Reference format:  VAR_NAME=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# Find a reference in the 1Password app: right-click a field → "Copy Secret Reference".

# EXAMPLE_API_KEY=op://Private/Example Service/credential
# ANOTHER_TOKEN=op://Private/Some API/token
